<title>AUSTRALIA: Reserve Bank of Australia commodity index up.</title>
<headline>Reserve Bank of Australia commodity index up.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of Australia said its index of commodity prices rose by 1.2 percent in Special Drawing Rights (SDR) terms in January after rising 0.6 percent in December.</p>
<p>Rises in the prices of wool, aluminium and copper were partly offset by a fall in the price of gold, the bank said.</p>
<p>In Australian dollar terms, the index rose by 2.2 percent in January after a 0.4 percent fall in December.</p>
<p>The Reserve Bank indices were as follows (base 1989/90):</p>
<p>		     All Items		    Rural Component</p>
<p>		A$	SDR	US$	   A$	SDR	US$</p>
<p>Jan 97 p  92.1     84.8     93.3	 81.4     74.9     82.4</p>
<p>Dec 96 r  90.1     83.8     93.4	 79.0     73.5     81.9</p>
<p>Jan 96    97.1     82.3     93.6	 87.0     73.7     83.8</p>
<p>		 Non-Rural Component     of which: Base Metals</p>
<p>		A$	SDR	US$	  A$	 SDR	US$</p>
<p>Jan 97 p  98.7     90.8     99.9	88.6	81.5     89.7</p>
<p>Dec 96 r  96.8     90.0    100.3	82.1	76.3     85.1</p>
<p>Jan 96   102.6     86.9     98.9	95.3	80.7     91.9</p>
<p>NOTE - r = revised, p = preliminary  </p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
